														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3964580">
									

<p>Sorry, but this is a solid downvote from me. It just feels stale - the central anomaly is a fairly by-the-numbers memetic hazard, and the addendums (breach log, interview, horror word salad lyrics document, and GoI stinger) are all pretty generic. It's not going beyond the comfortable tropes of SCP format, and it never goes anywhere I'm not expecting.</p>
<p>The article's structure is kind of confused, as if the article is talking in circles around the effect rather than explaining it straightforwardly (particularly in the opening of the description - why not just say it is a cognitohazardous/memetic hazard song, rather than an 'auditory phenomenon&#8230;' etc.?), and has weird gaps in it as a result. There's no explanation of -1's whereabouts pre-containment, no seeming interest how the researcher might have been infected, and no info on the speakers. AWCY? also seem shoe-horned in in a way that doesn't really add anything, like they could have been replaced entirely with another group (Fifthists, or some bespoke cult/group) and it wouldn't have changed anything, and the article seems to be bringing them in purely to provide a sense of escalation for the 'sting' at the end of the article.</p>

