			<div class="content" id="post-content-3964992">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Long&nbsp;crit.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">:.|:;</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Ok so we've got a song made by AWCY that warns people about a demonic entity or something.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Individuals who hear SCP-4150 in full feel a powerful urge to reproduce SCP-4150 (vocally or otherwise) and pass its effect to as many other individuals as possible.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Is that it? Because later one you say that it also tells people about something bad that's coming. Does nobody infected take a second to sit down and explain &quot;Hey I'm singing this so the world doesn't end&quot;. If it <em>is</em> just making people spread it against their will doesn't seem like a warning as much as an annoyance. Up until the interview there's nothing that implies that it's a warning and contradicts it very heavily.</p>
<p>Is SCP-4150-1 lying about it being a message? If you're trying to plant seeds of doubt here it's not working, It's just being confusing.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Penny Lane issn'a threat. It’s a warning. I told ya. There’s things out there you won't never be prepared for. And they’re comin’. Foundation or no.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Again, If this is true <em>why doesn't he tell anybody what this is</em>. Out of universe it just seems like you're making it vague. And that's not good for suspension of disbelief/immersion/etc. Not every villain needs to be sympathetic or have good intentions. Especially not AWCY. AWCY is crazy and has vague goals about chaos, That's it and that's what makes them so scary. Having a disturbing motivation can be much more important than having disturbing things happen.</p>
<p>Which of these is scarier:</p>
<ul>
<li>A man kills his roomate for insurance fraud.</li>
<li>A man tries and fails to kill his roommate because he finds dead people without eyes extremely attractive.</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>Shortly after the conclusion of this interview, it became apparent that SCP-4150-1 had stolen Researcher Roth’s pen, with which he stabbed himself in the neck. Subject died a week later on 05/02/2018. The phrase “PENNY LANE IS IN MY EARS AND IN MY EYES” was scrawled on the wall of his cell in blood.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Okay putting aside how the hell the foundation even let this happen <em>why</em> the hell did this even happen? Nothing he does indicates anything close to self mutilation and writing in blood. Was he trying to be profound? With stuff he already said&#8230;? He had a damn pen couldn't he write with that?<br />
This whole section comes out of nowhere and is frankly cheesy as hell. Jamming a guy killing himself and blood in at the end isn't scary it's just kinda gross and confusing. It doesn't work as &quot;shocking&quot; or &quot;edgy&quot; either since it's on the same site that calmly explains forced autocannibalism and fucked up incest cults. Maybe in a void that would be shocking but it isn't on the wiki.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>In conclusion this fails because:</p>
<ul>
<li>Like Rioghail mentioned there's very little this does that isn't done elsewhere.</li>
<li>A poor understanding of how terrorists think.</li>
<li>Inconsistency what it actually <em>does</em>.</li>
<li>That ending that just seems to be shock value.</li>
</ul>
<p>I do like that they seem to have control on things up until the ending though, Having it spread to the interviewer or having the guy suddenly kill him is not nearly as good as just having him kinda sit and say crazy things.</p>

							</div>

								
