<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;A&nbsp;brief&nbsp;response!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Minimise</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>&quot;Neutralised&quot; is correct spelling in the UK, where I'm from. I'd assume Researcher Roth is also from the UK. &quot;Lockbox&quot; is also valid spelling, and one in fact used on this site. For a couple of examples see 3714 and 3072.</p>
<p>Listening implies that the people are actively paying attention, whereas hearing is something more passive. In this scenario the people do not have to be actively paying attention, it simply has to register.</p>
<p>This criticism of my wording is ultimately subjective and I used the version I did for the sake of concision. It conveys the same information, but certainly if you felt it wasn't precise enough that's fair.</p>
<p>I decided not to consider them 4150-X instances because the SCP behaves like a contagion; admittedly it's a fine line but it's the difference between the SCP having an effect on people and the SCP turning people into anomalies.</p>
<p>-01 killed himself because after the second interview it became apparent that the interviewer knew about his AWCY connections - prior to this he was pretending to know nothing, and presumably preferred to stay in a cell rather than die. Once it became clear that he knew more than he was letting on, he feared the Foundation would attempt to coerce that information out of him, so he killed himself. If this seems extreme, well, he's an extremist. I think you'd agree he seems highly unstable. Then again, if that didn't click when you read it, that could easily be poor communication on my end.</p>
<p>Other than this, I'll concede that the premise isn't original, but the focus was meant to be on the story created through that. If it landed for you or if it didn't, thank you for reading nonetheless. Basically:</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I already changed the date format to be American, dammit, I don't want to change my spelling too!</p>

